{
  "name": "grease-bench",
  "description": "A minimalist resource monitoring tool implemented in runtimeless Rust that interfaces directly with the Linux kernel via raw x86-64 syscalls and inline assembly. It utilizes Linux Control Groups (cgroups) to isolate target processes and sample high-frequency memory usage statistics with minimal runtime interference. The architecture avoids standard library overhead by reimplementing core POSIX primitives for I/O, process management, and signal handling.",
